	<key>NSCameraUsageDescription</key>
	<string>Drivemate uses the camera to capture selfie photos for user profile verification and to scan QR codes for program attendance tracking. For example, when you attend a program event, you can scan a QR code to mark your attendance, or upload a selfie photo to verify your identity for membership purposes.</string>
	<key>NSContactsUsageDescription</key>
	<string>Drivemate needs access to your contacts so you can refer friends and earn rewards from the Refer &amp; Earn feature.</string>
	<key>NSLocalNetworkUsageDescription</key>
	<string>Drivemate needs local network access during development to connect to the Metro bundler on your Mac.</string>
